From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 21:01:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] uapi: drop the sockaddr_storage alias that collides with A13
 bionic

libbt-vendor (and anything else seeing both the exported kernel headers and
bionic) fails to compile on lineage-20.0:

  bionic/libc/include/sys/socket.h:73:8: error: redefinition of
    '__kernel_sockaddr_storage'
  .../generated_kernel_includes/gen/usr/include/linux/socket.h:24:26:
    note: expanded from macro 'sockaddr_storage'

This header defined struct __kernel_sockaddr_storage and then aliased
sockaddr_storage onto it for userspace, because bionic used to have no
definition of its own -- Android 12.1's sys/socket.h mentions
sockaddr_storage nowhere at all, which is why the identical kernel builds
fine on 19.1. Android 13's bionic declares struct sockaddr_storage itself,
so the alias turns that declaration into a redefinition.

Removed the alias, matching what upstream Linux later did. The struct
definition is untouched, and the block was already #ifndef __KERNEL__, so
kernel-internal builds are unaffected.
---
 include/uapi/linux/socket.h | 20 +++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/uapi/linux/socket.h b/include/uapi/linux/socket.h
index 359c82ac38f..b42153b4cbc 100644
--- a/include/uapi/linux/socket.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/socket.h
@@ -19,10 +19,20 @@ struct __kernel_sockaddr_storage {
 } __attribute__ ((aligned(_K_SS_ALIGNSIZE)));	/* force desired alignment */
 
 
-#ifndef __KERNEL__
-/* This header is exposed as linux/socket.h, so it must provide definition
- * for sockaddr_storage in place of include/linux/socket.h */
-#define sockaddr_storage __kernel_sockaddr_storage
-#endif
+/*
+ * ether/Android 13: the "#define sockaddr_storage __kernel_sockaddr_storage" that used to
+ * live here has been removed.
+ *
+ * It existed so userspace including <linux/socket.h> got a sockaddr_storage, because bionic
+ * did not define one. That changed in Android 13: bionic's sys/socket.h now declares
+ * "struct sockaddr_storage" itself. With the macro still in place the preprocessor rewrites
+ * that declaration into "struct __kernel_sockaddr_storage", which this header already
+ * defined above, so every translation unit that sees both headers fails with:
+ *
+ *   bionic/libc/include/sys/socket.h:73: error: redefinition of '__kernel_sockaddr_storage'
+ *
+ * Upstream Linux dropped the same macro for the same reason. Android 12.1 was unaffected
+ * only because its bionic had no sockaddr_storage of its own.
+ */
 
 #endif /* _UAPI_LINUX_SOCKET_H */
